<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21288] lnet: discovery-off push deletes a configured peer</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21288</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;A push from a peer with discovery off can delete a peer that the user configured with &lt;tt&gt;lnetctl peer add&lt;/tt&gt;. A ping reply with the same content does not delete that peer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Problem"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Problem&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;lnet_discovery_event_reply()&lt;/tt&gt; keeps a peer that has &lt;tt&gt;LNET_PEER_CONFIGURED&lt;/tt&gt; set. &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-14661" title="Provide kernel API for adding peer/peer NI" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-14661"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-14661&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; added this rule. The matching check in &lt;tt&gt;lnet_peer_push_event()&lt;/tt&gt; is older than &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-14661" title="Provide kernel API for adding peer/peer NI" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-14661"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-14661&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, and it does not test &lt;tt&gt;LNET_PEER_CONFIGURED&lt;/tt&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;&lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (!(lp-&amp;gt;lp_state &amp;amp; (LNET_PEER_NO_DISCOVERY |
                      LNET_PEER_LOCK_PRIMARY |
                      LNET_PEER_DISCOVERING)) &amp;amp;&amp;amp;
     lp-&amp;gt;lp_state &amp;amp; LNET_PEER_DISCOVERED) {
        ...
        lp-&amp;gt;lp_state |= LNET_PEER_MARK_DELETION;
}
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The sequence:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The user adds a peer with &lt;tt&gt;lnetctl peer add&lt;/tt&gt;. Discovery on the local node then discovers the peer.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The remote node turns discovery off. &lt;tt&gt;lnet_set_peer_discovery()&lt;/tt&gt; calls &lt;tt&gt;lnet_push_update_to_peers(1)&lt;/tt&gt;, and the remote node pushes to its Multi-Rail peers.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;lnet_peer_push_event()&lt;/tt&gt; on the local node sets &lt;tt&gt;LNET_PEER_MARK_DELETION&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The discovery thread calls &lt;tt&gt;lnet_peer_deletion()&lt;/tt&gt;, which calls &lt;tt&gt;lnet_peer_del_locked()&lt;/tt&gt;. That function deletes the configured peer and all its peer NIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;The local node thus loses the user configuration. Traffic later creates a new peer that has no &lt;tt&gt;LNET_PEER_CONFIGURED&lt;/tt&gt; flag and none of the configured NIDs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Proposedfix"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Proposed fix&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Add &lt;tt&gt;LNET_PEER_CONFIGURED&lt;/tt&gt; to the push check, so that both paths keep a configured peer. Add a test that configures a peer on a second node, discovers it, turns discovery off on that node, and checks that the peer stays.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Source"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Source&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Gerrit AI review found this case on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/70549" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/70549&lt;/a&gt; (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21145" title="'network' target mount option does not work with LNet dynamic peer discovery" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-21145"&gt;LU-21145&lt;/a&gt;), which changes the same check. The finding is from the source only. Nobody has reproduced it at runtime yet.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
